---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Pricing | Podomy"
	description="Podomy commercial licenses start at $10,000 USD per year. Enterprise deployments are quoted individually. SLAs and support are priced separately."
	currentPath="/pricing/"
>
	<h1 class="page-title">Pricing</h1>
	<p class="page-lead">
		Clear numbers, no sales maze.
	</p>

	<section class="content-section" style="margin-top: 0;">
		<p class="body-p">
			If you want to keep your code closed, you buy a license. If you are happy staying open, it is free under AGPLv3.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Open Source: $0</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			AGPLv3. Free to use, modify, and distribute, provided derivative work stays open under the same license. Built for open-source projects, research, and evaluation.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Commercial: from $10,000 per year</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			For companies making under $1,000,000 a year, including those embedding our software into proprietary products. Startups, research spin-outs, and small teams are welcome at the floor price.
		</p>
		<ul class="bullet-list">
			<li>A commercial license without AGPLv3 copyleft obligations.</li>
			<li>Pilots, small fleets, and internal tooling.</li>
			<li>Access to updates and bug fixes for the licensed version.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Enterprise: quoted individually</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			For companies making over $1,000,000 a year. The quote depends on how many machines you run, and whether you need warranty, indemnity, or SLAs.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Try it first</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			Concord is a single binary. Install it, run two nodes on a laptop, and partition the network yourself. The <a href="/docs/deployment/" class="body-link">deployment guide</a> walks through it.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Support and SLAs</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			Support is separate from licensing at every tier. Whether you pay the floor price or an enterprise quote, you decide what level of support you need.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Contact</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			Tell us about your deployment and we will tell you which side of the line you are on. <a href="/contact/" class="body-link">Contact engineering</a>
		</p>
	</section>
</Layout>
